# TD-01. These two are excluded from the BUILD CONTEXT, so no stage can copy them even by accident.
#
#   config_atlas.json is the live provider config. `scripts/build-images.sh` builds from the working
#   tree, so without this line a local build baked whatever provider key sat there into four images
#   — and ADR 0002 claimed the opposite ("a provider token is the only secret in the deployment […]
#   excluded by both .gitignore and .dockerignore"). The .gitignore half was true.
#
#   config_palmares_validators.json is not a secret — it is five public script hashes — but baking it
#   ships a snapshot that the next deploy makes wrong, which is exactly how the Belt System came to
#   have a committed validator config whose minting-policy hash matched nothing.
#
# Neither is needed to build: `extra-source-files` lists only config/reconcile-*. At run time both
# arrive by env (ATLAS_CORE_CONFIG, DEPLOYED_VALIDATORS_CONFIG) or by the bind mount compose makes.
config/config_atlas.json
config/config_palmares_validators.json
docs
*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store
